[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2609051700-orphan-audit-a-permanent-exit-2-that-told-you-to-retry"
  :adr/title "west-orphan-audit: a permanent exit 2 whose printed remedy was to re-run"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-09-05"
  :adr/related ["ADR-2608230300" "ADR-2608136000"]
  :adr/context
  "Found during a cleanup pass. `nbb scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljs` exited 2 with: GitHub に後継を訊けなかった候補が 1 件 … gh が答えられる状態で再実行すること. gh was working; every other lookup in the same run answered.

The candidate was orgs/kotoba-cli-verify-120601/repo, whose origin is a local filesystem path left by the kotoba-cli build verifier (/Users/…/runs/kotoba-cli-build-verifier/cloud-murakumo-20260903-115727/repo). `canonical-slug` correctly reported that this is not a github.com URL, but the caller wrapped every unverified result as `(assoc … :kind :ask-failed)`, so a remote that is structurally unaskable was counted as a transient gh failure.

The script's own docstring already draws the distinction it then discarded: :ask-failed is temporary and drives exit 2; :no-remote is structural and deliberately does NOT, because a permanent exit 2 only manufactures an always-red detector nobody can act on. A non-GitHub remote is the :no-remote case wearing a URL."
  :adr/decision
  "canonical-slug returns :kind :non-github-remote for a remote that is not a github.com URL, and the reducer respects a kind the classifier already stated instead of overwriting it. The class is counted, printed and excluded from exit 2 alongside :no-remote, and the advice line is now conditional: re-run is printed only when something actually failed to answer; the structural classes are told, in their own line, that re-running changes nothing and the row must be classified by hand.

Verified in both directions on the live tree, not only in argument: with working auth the run exits 0 and prints `ask-failed=0 no-remote=1 non-github-remote=1`; with GH_TOKEN set to an invalid token the same code exits 2 with `ask-failed=29` and the re-run advice. The failing direction had to be provoked deliberately, because the whole defect was that the two directions looked identical from the outside."
  :adr/consequences
  "The 6-hourly detector (:verify-west-registration-gap) runs --findings, which never calls gh, so its exit semantics are unchanged. What changes is the human and CI path: exit 2 from this audit again means a run that could not answer, rather than a fixed property of the tree.

orgs/kotoba-cli-verify-120601/repo is still unclassified on purpose. It is verifier scratch with one dirty file and local commits whose only remote is a local path; the rules forbid registering or retiring an unverified row, and it is now reported as structurally unverifiable rather than as a failure to retry."
  :adr/tags ["cleanup" "west" "detector" "evidence-floor"]}]
